WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.470 --> 00:00:04.640
The big cover up
Where I come from

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:07.930
there was always been a need for women who
take a stand.

00:00:07.930 --> 00:00:11.150
As a child in Afghanistan,
I used to watch my mother read the news on

00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:12.280
public TV.

00:00:12.280 --> 00:00:14.540
But when the Mujaheddin fighters came into
power

00:00:14.540 --> 00:00:17.789
in the early nineties
the acting Communist government

00:00:17.789 --> 00:00:21.089
started to make admissions to the Islamist
opposition.

00:00:21.089 --> 00:00:24.990
They ordered all female anchors to wear a
headscarf on TV.

00:00:24.990 --> 00:00:26.499
My mother refused to do this.

00:00:26.499 --> 00:00:30.029
Political conflicts shouldn’t be settled
over the rights of women.

00:00:30.029 --> 00:00:34.910
Against all odds and the pressure of the government
she went on-air, headscarf free.

00:00:34.910 --> 00:00:38.400
Until today her act of resilience
inspires me immensely.

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:41.960
This is one of the reasons
that I chose journalism as a profession.

00:00:41.960 --> 00:00:46.930
If you take a stand
you can have an enormous impact on society.

00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:49.490
Headscarf or no headscarf,
you should decide for yourself

00:00:49.490 --> 00:00:51.070
what you want to wear.

00:00:51.070 --> 00:00:54.750
I'm Waslat Hasrat-Nazimi
and I work at DW.

